// # Library Split Handoff — Three Oversized Std Files
//
// Logline: Hand off the 256-line-cap split of btree_disk_ops, protein_translation, and dispatch_worker to the library lane.
//
// Setup: Audit lane owns board state and library_status.oot. Library lane (agy) owns std/*.oo edits. This spec is durable, not a script.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Per-file seam analysis with file:line evidence.
//   2. Door-and-siblings split proposals mirroring library_status.oot and std/ naming.
//   3. Per-sibling line budget and acceptance test.
//   4. Cross-reference: prove status (BLOCKED) is unchanged by file size.

// ## 1. Why split (file:line evidence)
//
// FORMAT.oot:20: "Line limit: Every `.oo` and `.oot` file must not exceed 256 lines. Comments count."
// FORMAT.oot:56: "256-line constraint: Comments count toward the 256-line limit. Split files only along natural domain seams."
// FORMAT.oot:92: "Line limit: Strictly <= 256 lines per `.oot` document."
// library_status.oot:7: "files 4476  GREEN 2844  BLOCKED 1572  RESIDUAL 60  UNCHECKED 0".
// library_status.oot:13-19: top BLOCKED needs are oodac gaps, not file size.
//
// The three target files (btree_disk_ops.oo = 395, protein_translation.oo = 380, dispatch_worker.oo = 323)
// are all BLOCKED. Splitting reduces line count only. Prove status stays BLOCKED.

// ## 2. Door-and-siblings pattern (reference)
//
// library_status.oot:21-44: door summarises, 21 sibling tails continue the table.
// std mirrors the same shape:
//   dispatch.oo (door) + dispatch_types.oo, dispatch_worker.oo, dispatch_engine.oo, dispatch_stubs.oo.
//   database.oo (door) + database_<role>.oo (siblings).
// Pattern rule for the three splits:
//   <topic>.oo          = door (header + thin re-export via imports).
//   <topic>_<role>.oo   = sibling (one role per file; <= 256 lines).
// Sibling naming follows the existing std pattern (types, ops, scan, node, task).

// ## 3. btree_disk_ops.oo (395 lines)
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-12    Academy header.
//   Line 13       import "./btree_disk_types.oo";.
//   Lines 15-29   btree_node_key_at (slot accessor).
//   Lines 31-45   btree_node_val_at (slot accessor).
//   Lines 47-58   btree_node_find_key_index (binary search).
//   Lines 60-74   btree_node_lookup_value (read).
//   Lines 76-225  btree_node_insert_key_value (insert; n=0/1/2/3 cases).
//   Lines 227-300 btree_node_split_leaf (split; single fn).
//   Lines 302-395 btree_node_remove_key (remove; n=0/1/2/3 cases).
//
// Domain seams:
//   A. Lookup and accessors — lines 15-74  (read paths only).
//   B. Insert               — lines 76-225 (mutate; n-state case expansion).
//   C. Split                — lines 227-300 (BTreeSplit producer).
//   D. Remove               — lines 302-395 (mutate; n-state case expansion).
//
// Proposed split (1 door + 4 siblings):
//
// | Sibling                    | Role      | Body lines | Total w/ header |
// |----------------------------|-----------|------------|------------------|
// | btree_disk_ops.oo (door)   | re-export | 4 imports  | ~16              |
// | btree_disk_ops_lookup.oo   | A         | 60 + 3     | ~75              |
// | btree_disk_ops_insert.oo   | B         | 150 + 3    | ~165             |
// | btree_disk_ops_split.oo    | C         | 74 + 3     | ~89              |
// | btree_disk_ops_remove.oo   | D         | 94 + 3     | ~109             |
//
// All <= 256 lines. Overhead = 5 Academy headers (~60 lines) and the door re-export.
// btree_disk_ops.oo stays as the door because it is the established import path; siblings are
// sub-roles of "ops", same shape as dispatch_worker.oo holding worker ops under dispatch.oo.
//
// Acceptance test:
//   1. oodac check on each new sibling and the door; expect clean emit.
//   2. All 7 public symbols stay importable from btree_disk_ops.oo:
//      btree_node_key_at, btree_node_val_at, btree_node_find_key_index,
//      btree_node_lookup_value, btree_node_insert_key_value,
//      btree_node_split_leaf, btree_node_remove_key.
//   3. No new imports beyond line 13 of the original (`./btree_disk_types.oo`).
//   4. Prove status stays BLOCKED. library_status.oot row unchanged in column 5.

// ## 4. protein_translation.oo (380 lines)
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-12     Academy header.
//   Lines 14-20    type ProteinSequence.
//   Lines 22-29    type OrfRecord.
//   Lines 31-38    type TranslateAcc.
//   Lines 40-52    int_pow4, int_pow32.
//   Lines 54-72    dna_base_at, dna_pack4, codon_pack, codon_at.
//   Lines 74-175   codon_standard_aa (NCBI table 1; ~100-line switch).
//   Lines 177-195  codon_is_start_standard, codon_is_stop_standard.
//   Lines 197-262  protein_aa_weight_da (residue mass switch).
//   Lines 264-278  protein_aa_charge (KR+/DE-).
//   Lines 280-338  translate_empty, translate_scan, protein_translate_frame,
//                  protein_translate_nucleotides, protein_estimate_molecular_weight,
//                  protein_estimate_net_charge.
//   Lines 340-380  protein_sequence_new, protein_sequence_mw, protein_sequence_charge,
//                  protein_orf_new, orf_is_complete.
//
// Domain seams:
//   A. Types and bit-pack utils — lines 14-72   (3 types + 7 pack helpers).
//   B. Codon table              — lines 74-195  (standard_aa + is_start + is_stop).
//   C. AA properties            — lines 197-278 (weight_da + charge).
//   D. Translation scan         — lines 280-338 (translate_empty, scan, frame, nucleotides, estimate_*).
//   E. Sequence and ORF records — lines 340-380 (sequence_*, orf_new, is_complete).
//
// Proposed split (1 door + 4 siblings):
//
// | Sibling                            | Role      | Body lines | Total w/ header |
// |------------------------------------|-----------|------------|------------------|
// | protein_translation.oo (door)      | re-export | 5 imports  | ~17              |
// | protein_translation_types.oo       | A         | ~60        | ~75              |
// | protein_translation_codons.oo      | B         | ~120       | ~135             |
// | protein_translation_aa.oo          | C         | ~80        | ~95              |
// | protein_translation_scan.oo        | D         | ~60        | ~75              |
// | protein_translation_seq.oo         | E         | ~45        | ~60              |
//
// All <= 256 lines. codon_table.oo already exists in ooda/std/bioinformatics/ (the lookup table);
// protein_translation_codons.oo holds the AA decoding and start/stop predicates. Do NOT shadow it.
//
// Acceptance test:
//   1. oodac check on each new sibling and the door; expect clean emit.
//   2. All 23 public symbols stay importable from protein_translation.oo.
//   3. The 3 type defs (ProteinSequence, OrfRecord, TranslateAcc) declared exactly once in *_types.oo.
//   4. Prove status stays BLOCKED. library_status.oot row unchanged in column 5.

// ## 5. dispatch_worker.oo (323 lines)
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-4     Academy header (minimal).
//   Lines 6-12    type DispatcherConfig.
//   Lines 14-23   type SwarmDispatcher.
//   Lines 25-34   type WorkerNode.
//   Lines 36-47   type SwarmTask.
//   Lines 49-80   dispatcher_config_init.
//   Lines 82-93   dispatcher_init.
//   Lines 95-110  worker_node_init.
//   Lines 112-125 swarm_task_create.
//   Lines 127-228 worker_node_can_accept, assign, release, update_status, heartbeat.
//   Lines 230-323 task_is_terminal, can_retry, mark_dispatched, mark_completed,
//                 mark_failed, mark_cancelled.
//
// Domain seams:
//   A. Types and lifecycle ctors   — lines 6-125   (4 types + 4 init/create fns).
//   B. Worker-node state machine   — lines 127-228 (5 worker ops).
//   C. Task state machine          — lines 230-323 (6 task ops).
//
// Conflict note: type DispatcherConfig is declared in dispatch_worker.oo:6-12 AND dispatch_types.oo:6-9.
// Library lane must dedupe during the split. Canonical def lives in dispatch_types.oo;
// dispatch_worker_types.oo imports it instead of redeclaring.
//
// Proposed split (1 door + 3 siblings):
//
// | Sibling                      | Role      | Body lines | Total w/ header |
// |------------------------------|-----------|------------|------------------|
// | dispatch_worker.oo (door)    | re-export | 3 imports  | ~15              |
// | dispatch_worker_types.oo     | A         | ~120       | ~135             |
// | dispatch_worker_node.oo      | B         | ~115       | ~130             |
// | dispatch_worker_task.oo      | C         | ~95        | ~110             |
//
// All <= 256 lines. dispatch_worker_types.oo reuses the canonical DispatcherConfig from
// dispatch_types.oo:6-9 via `import "./dispatch_types.oo";`.
//
// Acceptance test:
//   1. oodac check on each new sibling and the door; expect clean emit.
//   2. All 17 public symbols stay importable from dispatch_worker.oo.
//   3. type DispatcherConfig declared exactly once. oodac must not report "redefinition".
//   4. Prove status stays BLOCKED. library_status.oot row unchanged in column 5.

// ## 6. Cross-reference to library_status.oot
//
// The 3 target files are in the BLOCKED set per library_status.oot:7.
// Recent commits of the form "audit: GREEN N BLOCKED M" toggle row counts (audit lane, not library).
// BLOCKED cause is oodac (library_status.oot:13-19), not file size.
//
// After the split:
//   - btree_disk_ops.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
//   - protein_translation.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
//   - dispatch_worker.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
//
// Audit lane will refresh library_status.oot and library_status_tail_*.oot row entries; this is
// expected. Library lane must not re-attribute BLOCKED to file size in the new rows.

// ## 7. Out of scope and constraints
//
// Out of scope for the library lane:
//   - Editing btree_disk_types.oo, dispatch_types.oo, codon_table.oo, or any other std file.
//   - Re-running prove (audit/prove_helpers/* owns prove).
//   - Editing library_status.oot or its tails (audit lane owns the door).
//   - Renaming public symbols; this is a pure file move, not an API change.
//
// Constraints (per FORMAT.oot sections 1-2):
//   - 4-element Academy header on every new sibling (FORMAT.oot:31-41).
//   - <= 256 lines per file (FORMAT.oot:20).
//   - No new imports beyond what the originals already use. protein_translation.oo and
//     dispatch_worker.oo currently import nothing of their own; btree_disk_ops.oo imports only
//     btree_disk_types.oo (line 13).
//   - ASD-STE100 prose (FORMAT.oot:80-83, RULES.oot 1.10).
//
// Handoff complete when:
//   - 12 new sibling .oo files exist (4 btree + 5 protein + 3 dispatch) plus 3 slimmed doors.
//   - All 15 files <= 256 lines.
//   - oodac check clean on every new file.
//   - library_status.oot BLOCKED rows still present, cause still oodac.
